## Methodology

Soil moisture is expressed as a percentile rank (0–1) from the AWRA-L v7 decile product, calibrated against the full 1911–present historical record for each location and season. A composite stress index combines soil moisture deficit ({{ dryness_weight_pct }}% weight), vapour pressure deficit ({{ vpd_weight_pct }}%), and maximum temperature ({{ temperature_weight_pct }}%), normalised against configured critical references ({{ critical_temp_threshold }} °C; {{ critical_vpd_threshold_kpa }} kPa VPD). Risk levels are assigned from the stress index: Critical ≥ {{ critical_risk_threshold }}, Alert {{ alert_risk_threshold }}–<{{ critical_risk_threshold }}, Watch {{ watch_risk_threshold }}–<{{ alert_risk_threshold }}, Low < {{ watch_risk_threshold }}. This product describes conditions relative to historical norms — it is not a forecast of future rainfall and does not constitute a formal drought declaration.

## Caveats

- Grid-cell resolution is 0.05° (~5 km). Conditions at individual paddock or property scale may differ materially.
- Soil moisture reflects the AWRA-L model estimate, not direct field measurement.
- Temperature and VPD are averaged over the selected period; short-duration heatwave events within the period may be damped.
- This bulletin is for situational awareness only. Formal drought declarations follow separate DPIRD processes.

